The rotate residual stopped before slicing: K does not relate the hook terms `SHIFT <=Int L` and `notBool(SHIFT >Int L)` when `L` is an opaque total length. I’m restating the complementary claim with the exact operational guard `notBool(SHIFT >Int L)`. This remains an exhaustive two-valued partition and avoids assuming an unproved solver normalization.
apply patch
