codex
A cleaner program-level solution avoids the problematic “concatenate two symbolic slices”: for `0 ≤ shift ≤ len(s)`, a right rotation is the single window `(s + s)[len(s)-shift : 2*len(s)-shift]`. I’m adopting that equivalent implementation, while preserving the canonical behavior for negative shifts (`s`) and the required oversized-shift reversal. Each path will be a complementary symbolic claim.
apply patch
patch: completed
/workspace/solution.py
